WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.180
- I'm Ron DeSantis and
I'm running for president

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.846
to lead our great American comeback.

00:00:05.846 --> 00:00:07.830
(intense music continues)

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.420
- [Narrator] Florida
governor, Ron DeSantis,

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.660
has officially entered the
2024 presidential race,

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.120
after announcing his bid
in a Twitter conversation

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.070
with Elon Musk.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.050
- [Ron] Governing is not entertainment.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.050
It's not about building a
brand or virtue signaling.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.600
It is about delivering results.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.780
And our results in Florida
have been second-to-none.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:32.760
We can and we must deliver
big results for America.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.260
- [Narrator] After a
big win in the midterms

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.720
and a successful legislative
session in Florida,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.080
DeSantis is looking to
take his politics national,

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.750
going head to head with
former president Donald Trump

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.760
for the GOP nomination.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.680
- They are the top two contenders

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.540
for the Republican
nomination at this point.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.890
No one else comes close.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.480
- [Narrator] But moving
from state politics

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.680
to a national stage

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.080
presents its own challenges for DeSantis.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.270
So what should we expect
from the governor,

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.073
and what challenges lie ahead?

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.040
(somber music)

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.300
Once close allies,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.760
the relationship between
DeSantis and Trump

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.650
has evolved greatly over time.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.790
- We need to elect Ron DeSantis

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.140
as your governor.
(crowd cheering)

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.660
- [Narrator] Trump endorsed DeSantis

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.370
in the 2018 gubernatorial election.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.250
- Mr. President, I look
forward to working with you

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.440
to advance Florida's priorities.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.360
I think you're gonna get
tired of me calling you,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.340
asking you for things for Florida.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.590
- They felt similarly on a lot of issues.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:31.980
DeSantis sort of championed
those issues back in Florida.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.930
The president had a real ally there.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.080
That really came off the wheels recently

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.750
as the governor asserted
himself politically

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.660
and began to look at a presidential run.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.820
- [Narrator] Now, Trump's
attitude toward DeSantis

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.070
has soured, often jabbing the governor

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.170
about sagging approval ratings.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:52.410
- Let's see, there it is, Trump at 71,

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:56.010
Ron DeSanctimonious at 10%.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.350
- He feels that the governor is disloyal,

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.950
that Ron DeSantis is not
showing him proper respect

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.383
by challenging him for the presidency.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:07.410
- [Narrator] DeSantis has
largely avoided responding

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.810
to the former president's attacks.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.610
- I don't know how to
spell DeSanctimonious.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.720
I don't really know what it means,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.010
but you know, I kinda like it.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.570
It's long, it's got a lotta vowels.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:16.440
I mean, so.
(Piers laughing)

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.790
We can go with that, that's fine.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.710
You know, you can call
me whatever you want.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.510
I mean, just as long as you, you know,

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.800
also call me a winner.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.620
- In order to win the
Republican nomination,

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.010
Ron DeSantis is going to need
a lot of Trump supporters.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.500
So alienating those with
hard-hitting attacks

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.840
against the former president
could turn those people off.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.370
- Donald Trump.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.200
- [Narrator] Since
winning the 2018 election,

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.400
DeSantis' popularity among
voters has exploded in Florida,

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.970
illustrated by his landslide
19-point reelection win

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.220
in the November midterms.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.110
And his popularity continued to grow

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:52.260
after he delivered several
conservative policy victories

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.080
during the last legislative
session in Florida.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.850
From restrictions on drag shows

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.210
to limiting spending on
diversity programs in colleges,

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:03.180
DeSantis' policies have
made national headlines

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.920
and will likely serve as the backbone

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.600
for his presidential campaign

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.720
as he tries to win over
a wider range of voters.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.610
- He'll be able to say,
"Look how effective I was.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.740
I got X, Y, and X done."

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.390
Versus, you know, some of the struggles

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:18.930
that Trump as president had
getting his agenda passed.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.640
- [Narrator] Other bills
endorsed by DeSantis

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.520
include allowing concealed
handguns without a permit

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.043
and a strick six-week abortion ban.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.490
While those policies
may serve DeSantis well

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.650
in the primaries, they could also prove

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:34.980
to be a challenge for him
in the general election.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.360
In a "Wall Street Journal" poll

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.880
asking about the right to
carry a concealed handgun

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.080
without a permit,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.690
56% of Republican primary voters

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.460
said they support that right.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:49.320
While nationwide, 65% of overall
voters were in opposition.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.090
And for the six-week abortion ban,

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:55.170
68% of Republican primary
voters favored the ban,

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:58.590
but 53% of voters overall opposed it.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.600
- The abortion issue is very complex.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.890
It's controversial.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:06.360
Six weeks is seen as pretty
extreme by a lot of people.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.980
- [Narrator] DeSantis is also preparing

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.380
to challenge the incumbent
president, Joe Biden,

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.600
who along with Trump
has experience running

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.913
in presidential elections
and winning them.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.350
- DeSantis is not tested
on a national stage.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.060
He doesn't have the experience dealing

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.780
with world leaders or major global issues.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.980
So that'll be something
that both Trump and Biden

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.560
would use against Ron DeSantis.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.600
- [Narrator] DeSantis
now joins a growing swath

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.610
of Republican candidates in the race,

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.980
including Trump, former
South Carolina governor,

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:41.040
Nikki Haley, and South
Carolina senator, Tim Scott,

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.420
with the potential for others,

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.730
including former vice
president Mike Pence,

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:47.160
who may announce in the coming months.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.880
- Right now, it's down to
Donald Trump and Ron DeSantis.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.070
It's their fight to lose.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.690
Republicans are hungry for someone

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.890
who can get something done.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.210
There's a number of other Republicans

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.796
that are vying for this and
they're gonna be looking

00:04:58.796 --> 00:05:01.950
especially to see if
Ron DeSantis stumbles.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:05.197
Essentially, if you boil down
Ron DeSantis' argument is,

00:05:05.197 --> 00:05:06.540
"I am effective.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.780
I can carry on the agenda that
Donald Trump kinda started

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.066
but actually get it passed."

00:05:11.066 --> 00:05:14.399
(light music continues)

